@startuml
title Logout — immediate local change, then credential cleanup
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #DBEAFE
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #93C5FD
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
actor User
participant "Auth controller" as Auth
participant "Session store" as Store
database "Storage adapter" as Storage
participant Backend
User -> Auth : signOut()
Auth -> Store : clear() immediately
Store -> Store : Advance generation\nAnonymous state blocks protected work
Store --> User : Protected workspace unavailable
Auth -> Auth : Wait for earlier auth operations
Auth -> Storage : Attempt pending = true
Auth -> Storage : Read refresh token\nDelete saved native token in finally
note over Auth,Storage
Web: read returns null; delete is a no-op.
Backend request uses the HttpOnly cookie.
Storage failure can leave cleanup/revocation unconfirmed.
end note
alt Credential read / deletion succeeded
  Auth -> Backend : Logout (native token / web cookie)
  alt Server success AND marker write succeeded
    Backend --> Auth : Success
    Auth -> Storage : Remove pending marker
  else Network / server failure OR earlier marker error
    Auth -> Store : reportError(revocation unconfirmed)
    note over Auth,Storage : Saved pending marker remains if not removed.
  end
else Credential read / deletion failed
  Auth -> Store : reportError(revocation unconfirmed)
end
note over User,Storage
App stays locally signed out on failure.
A saved pending marker blocks restoration on next startup.
No automatic logout retry worker is implemented.
end note
@enduml
